    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_70fb60e6e1cc48baa923817d124284f7de0ecbf59ba7f2a6b7c62ecffffc9a1c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source develops a discrete-to-continuum construction: separating component lengths from integer harmonics factors frequency counting into a geometric Dirichlet series times zeta; the Cantor string shows how self-similar length data become a lattice of pole-defined complex dimensions; continuum string and dual-string transforms are then proposed so that their quotient realizes zeta and reflection is represented as duality.",
