      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_961a169fc0888d85bb1bd887bb439b0767c31ec6ce8d09af8b1d1a87543cc380",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source stages a conditional rigidity strategy: a permutation audit first shows that the raw zeta and orthogonality symmetries leave generic off-critical cases; affine covariance under conjugation and reflection then imposes 2b+a=1 and the shared fixed point 1/2; finally, deformation within the constrained operator family is intended to turn discreteness of the zero set into critical-line rigidity.",
